NASA FIRMS
----------

Dataset: fire_detections (95,392 MODIS detections, presumed vegetation
fires, from 1 November 2019 to 31 January 2020 in New South Wales,
Victoria, the Australian Capital Territory and the Jervis Bay Territory;
52,865 of them rated 80 or more for confidence)

Publisher: NASA's Fire Information for Resource Management System (FIRMS),
part of LANCE and the Earth Science Data and Information System (ESDIS):
its yearly country files of the MODIS standard-quality detections
(MCD14ML, from Terra and Aqua; version 6.03 as the files give it), which
FIRMS's FAQ says are "a subset of the standard quality data processed by
the MODIS Fire Team Science Computing Facility at the University of
Maryland". The product's citation, as its DOI gives it: Giglio, L., MODIS
Thermal Anomalies/Fire Products, NASA LANCE FIRMS,
doi:10.5067/FIRMS/MODIS/MCD14ML.
https://firms.modaps.eosdis.nasa.gov/country/

